  "policy": "A gate FAILS when the current value is worse than baseline by more than the tolerance; the verification step then fails. Tolerances: quality 0.02 nDCG absolute; Core retrieval latency +50 % (measured run-to-run variance about 15 %); HTTP latency +100 % on 1000-request runs (few seconds, laptop noise), +50 % on the 1M-request gate; errors: none allowed. A FAIL needs either a fix or a new approved baseline with the reason recorded here. Benchmark-suite gates (kind 'bench') compare a run-benchmarks.py report (--bench) with the 2026-11-01 full run: throughput -30 %, latency +50 % (stress +100 %), soak errors none. Latency and throughput gates are marked hardware_bound: they apply only on the hardware named in 'hardware'. Another machine (QWENBRIDGE_PERF_HARDWARE, e.g. github-hosted-4cpu in the Master Verification workflow) reports them as NOT GATED with the measured value; quality and error gates apply on every machine. Scenario J on other hardware compares the slowed run with the same run (--rebase)."
